<?nvs
// The job `examples/queue-purge.nvs` enqueues so that it has a claimed row to
// ask about.
//
// [ADR 0153](/docs/decisions/0153.md) § 2: a claimed job is not removable at
// all, and `Core\Queue::delete` answering `false` is the only way a caller
// finds that out. A row is `Claimed` for exactly as long as this file runs, so
// the parent's question has to arrive inside that window — and the window is a
// whole second because the parent polls for the claim first and then sends a
// statement of its own to a server.
//
// It prints nothing, for the reason `receipt.nvs` gives: a worker runs this on
// the same process and the same stdout the parent program is writing its
// frozen output to.
Core\Time::sleep(1s);
